00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.140
And, man, your connection is not sounding
great.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.670
Am I the one with the bad connection today?

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.670
Very bad.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:46.670
I can hear everybody excellent.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.050
And you sound like you're talking through
a tin can.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.130
Let me I'm actually calling from a nuclear
submarine.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.220
Is this any better?

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.270
Yes, actually, a little bit.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.120
You know, at the end of the hallway.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.120
But it sounds good.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.610
Well, I actually am in a hallway, so that
makes sense.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:01.970
Listen, third party.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:02.970
OK.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:08.220
So I'm I don't believe that the two party
system best serves our interests.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:14.090
I think that, you know, the Republican and
Democratic Party represent really a quite

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.430
