00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:40.670
And in the short term, they will potentially
have the spoiler effect that it sounds like

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.299
you might be referring to from 2016.

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:46.119
Yep, totally.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:47.459
I'm calling from northern California.

00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:49.450
Sorry, I didn't mention that.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.929
That's OK.

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:51.929
OK.

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:55.600
All right, well, I hope I answered the question.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.609
I appreciate the phone call.

00:01:56.609 --> 00:02:01.399
I do think we are finally getting the phones
are working properly, which is exciting.

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:06.030
Let's go to our next caller from the nine,
seven, eight area code.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.270
Who's calling today from nine, seven, eight?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.769
And where are you calling from?

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:12.709
Hi, my name is Isaac.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:13.780
I'm calling from Massachusetts.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.959
This is just a phone number from Alabam, I
believe.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:18.959
Love it.

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:19.959
Okay.

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:22.150
I thought nine, seven, eight was Massachusetts,
but go ahead.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.500
Oh, I'll get my bad.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.709
So, yeah, here's my question.

00:02:26.709 --> 00:02:30.319
How do you feel about the current Black Lives
Matter movement?

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:32.980
And do you think it will lead to meaningful
change?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.840
And how do you feel about how the movement
currently doesn't have, like a current leader,

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.480
like a face to lead the movement?

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.670
Well, listen, I don't think it's my place
to say whether the movement should or shouldn't

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:48.120
have a face or a leader.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.690
That's really up.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.969
I don't even know to who because there's no
leader.

00:02:52.969 --> 00:02:56.829
But I feel like it's up to someone else to
decide.

00:02:56.829 --> 00:03:00.049
I consider myself Black Lives Matter adjacent.

00:03:00.049 --> 00:03:06.209
In so far as many of the goals of Black Lives
Matter are the same goals that I've been pushing

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:09.939
for on this program for a very long time.

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:16.640
My my qualms with Black Lives Matter as a
pseudo organization are on the record that

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.980
none of them, I think, will come as a surprise
to people since I've talked about them before.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:26.450
I believe that there was at the time when
the Black Lives Matter and Women's March were

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.770
sort of overlapping.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:35.560
I think they went in the wrong direction from
the standpoint of having anti Semitic associated

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.209
people speaking for them and organizing events.

00:03:39.209 --> 00:03:45.560
I think that the way in which some Black Lives
Matter chapters have thrown in with the anti

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.400
Israeli movement is self-defeating.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:57.010
And it's only going to alienate what is really
a natural natural ally, which is liberal American

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.010
Jews.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:03.180
I think that they are going to be alienated
by some of the anti Israeli language and stuff

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.861
about, you know, the fight for Palestine is
the same thing that that Blakley that, you

00:04:07.861 --> 00:04:11.269
know, we're fighting for here against police
brutality, cetera.

00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:13.850
You're starting to see really wacky stuff
come out.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:20.820
Like the reason police are a problem in the
US is because they got training from Israeli

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.600
officials on trips and, you know, like really,
really crazy stuff.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:31.010
So, you know, for me, I don't really get too
involved in the in the groups.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:33.890
And I've not even talked about this for probably
more than a year.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.380
But I'm glad you're bringing it up.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:41.070
But I am Black Lives Matter adjacent in that
I support a lot of the ideas that I think

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:46.000
most of the people support that are part of
Black Lives Matter.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.130
Great.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.260
Yeah.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:55.980
I believe, like the entire sentiment is very
like I feel like the public broadly approves

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.700
of what the spirit and sentiment is for Black
Lives Matter.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:00.700
Yes.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:06.821
But like, I feel like an immediate people
are portraying them as, you know, X, Y and

00:05:06.821 --> 00:05:07.821
Z.

00:05:07.821 --> 00:05:11.160
And I feel like that might like ruin the reputation
of the movement.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:18.000
I was just hoping that we could just move
forward and talk about what really matters

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.150
about this moment.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:24.100
Well, the thing is, what really matters to
you or to me might be different than what

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:29.910
matters, you know, to the people who are using
Black Lives Matter to push Israeli BTX versus

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:35.750
the people who are using black lives matter
to say, you know that what?

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:36.750
You know what?

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:37.750
Whatever.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:41.660
I think the whole point is there are things
that will have widespread agreement and then

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.800
there are areas where you start to lose people.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.890
And I would focus on the lowest hanging fruit
that can achieve the most meaningful change

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.820
with the biggest consensus.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.180
OK, great.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.800
Thank you so much for your comments.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.800
Glad to be on your show.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:57.800
Thank you so much.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:58.800
Thank you.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:05:59.800
Appreciate the phone call.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:05:59.805
Great to hear from you.

